   "text": "I read the structure region by region and assembled the SMILES below. I derived the stereocentres by hand from the wedges and hashes and did not run the SMILES through a parser.\n\n- **Cyclopropane amide:** a 2-methylcyclopropane carboxamide with the methyl wedged and the carbonyl hashed, i.e. trans. Both ring stereocentres work out as S.\n- **Alpha carbon:** it carries the hashed NH, a CH2 to the thiazole C2, and the carbonyl to the piperazic acid N1. I assigned it R.\n- **Piperazic ring:** a six-membered N\u2013NH ring running N1, NH, CH(C=O)O, CH2, CH2, CH2. The ring carbon bearing the ester is S, assuming the bond to NH is hashed.\n- **Ester linker:** the ester O\u2013CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2 connects back to indole C3.\n- **Thiazole and indole:** thiazole C4 is attached to indole C5. The indole has an N-ethyl group and its C2 is bonded to the pyridine.\n- **Pyridine:** C3 is bonded to the indole and C5 carries a 4-methylpiperazin-1-yl group. C2 bears a CH(CH3)OCH3 group with the methyl hashed, which I assigned S.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H]1C[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H]2Cc3nc(cs3)-c3ccc4c(c3)c(CC(C)(C)COC(=O)[C@@H]5CCCN(N5)C2=O)c(n4CC)-c2cc(N3CCN(C)CC3)cnc2[C@H](C)OC"
